00:18:06,200 --> 00:18:08,837
I'm so sorry Pops!

254
00:18:08,920 --> 00:18:11,640
forgive me Ace! please? Please!

255
00:18:19,980 --> 00:18:22,020
Hey, Secret!

256
00:18:25,460 --> 00:18:27,040
Pull it together.

257
00:18:27,520 --> 00:18:29,620
Tears won't fix what you've done.

258
00:18:38,120 --> 00:18:39,737
That old man's tough.

259
00:18:39,820 --> 00:18:41,996
He gets stabbed and he's still at it!

260
00:18:42,380 --> 00:18:44,800
I gotta get serious and save Ace!

261
00:18:45,240 --> 00:18:46,140
Off we go!

262
00:18:47,500 --> 00:18:48,840
Hey, Gene Bay!

263
00:18:49,720 --> 00:18:52,000
Doesn't that strike you as odd?

264
00:19:12,400 --> 00:19:17,282
They all abandoned their posts and retreated
to the plaza while we weren't looking.

265
00:19:17,480 --> 00:19:18,310
Hmm.

266
00:19:18,393 --> 00:19:19,757
Indeed, that is a bit troubling.

267
00:19:19,840 --> 00:19:22,177
But old white beard has
joined the fray now.

268
00:19:22,260 --> 00:19:24,495
That ought to put our worries to rest.

269
00:19:24,980 --> 00:19:25,810
True.

270
00:19:25,900 --> 00:19:29,018
We can handle whatever dirty
tricks they throw at us.

271
00:19:30,280 --> 00:19:31,760
Fire on the walls up.

272
00:19:32,440 --> 00:19:33,440
I'm sorry, sir.

273
00:19:33,560 --> 00:19:34,390
We're trying.

274
00:19:34,473 --> 00:19:36,847
But the ice is a lot
thicker than we thought.

275
00:19:48,880 --> 00:19:50,140
I'll make you pay!

276
00:19:51,260 --> 00:19:53,057
The wall is the crux of our plan.

277
00:19:53,140 --> 00:19:54,020
This is bad.

278
00:19:54,660 --> 00:19:57,248
I'm gonna buy us some
time till they fix it.

279
00:20:06,740 --> 00:20:08,237
That's as far as you're gonna get.

280
00:20:08,320 --> 00:20:10,140
You'll never reach the plaza!

281
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:14,830
Run!

282
00:20:15,020 --> 00:20:17,160
My Sandmo John Giant is attacking!

283
00:20:28,300 --> 00:20:31,180
You're blocking my view. Move.

284
00:20:54,440 --> 00:20:56,600
What did he do?

285
00:20:57,340 --> 00:20:58,680
Vice Admiral!

286
00:20:59,400 --> 00:21:00,230
What?

287
00:21:00,313 --> 00:21:01,569
Why is the ground tilting?

288
00:21:07,080 --> 00:21:09,720
Everyone, keep your distance from Pops!

289
00:21:10,100 --> 00:21:12,159
It's even worse than an earthquake!

290
00:21:22,440 --> 00:21:24,020
This can't be real.

291
00:21:24,380 --> 00:21:26,020
This is insane.

292
00:21:26,480 --> 00:21:28,260
It's not just the island.

293
00:21:28,620 --> 00:21:30,680
The entire sea is tilting.

294
00:21:51,760 --> 00:21:54,940
That old SOB sure got some style.

295
00:22:17,020 --> 00:22:18,200
I've got you!

296
00:22:21,120 --> 00:22:21,950
Jinbei!

297
00:22:22,560 --> 00:22:24,240
Hang on, I'll pull you up!

298
00:22:33,120 --> 00:22:34,160
Thanks, Team Bay.

299
00:22:34,440 --> 00:22:35,520
I owe you again.

300
00:22:35,980 --> 00:22:37,560
Take me when this is over.

301
00:22:38,500 --> 00:22:41,794
Is that crazy old man trying
to get his own crew killed?

302
00:22:42,140 --> 00:22:43,920
No, his crew was ready.

303
00:22:44,200 --> 00:22:46,259
They're used to this kind of thing.

304
00:22:52,360 --> 00:22:53,880
One man did this?

305
00:22:54,180 --> 00:22:56,600
He really is the strongest pirate alive.

306
00:23:02,560 --> 00:23:05,260
I've never seen such
fierce a power before,

307
00:23:05,640 --> 00:23:09,920
but in the name of the absolute
justice I've sworn to uphold,

308
00:23:10,220 --> 00:23:14,080
I'd rather die than let
you pass through here!

309
00:23:34,720 --> 00:23:36,300
It's headed right for us!

310
00:23:39,140 --> 00:23:41,434
The shockwave's gonna hit the scaffold!

311
00:23:41,820 --> 00:23:43,520
Yeah! Tear it apart!

312
00:23:56,100 --> 00:23:57,000
What happened?

313
00:23:57,320 --> 00:23:58,967
It looked like a direct hit.

314
00:23:59,840 --> 00:24:01,180
But did we get it?

315
00:24:06,100 --> 00:24:11,220
Doesn't look like it even touched the
scaffold so did something block the blast?

316
00:24:12,080 --> 00:24:13,297
Do you see that?

317
00:24:13,380 --> 00:24:17,680
It's the three admirals.

318
00:24:21,420 --> 00:24:24,637
This mess wouldn't have happened
if the walls were ready.

319
00:24:24,720 --> 00:24:26,297
Whose fault is that?

320
00:24:26,380 --> 00:24:27,917
Your ice is blocking them.

321
00:24:28,000 --> 00:24:32,537
Sure but you could have just
melted the ice couldn't you?

322
00:24:32,620 --> 00:24:34,437
Let's go.

323
00:24:34,520 --> 00:24:35,350
Give them hell!

324
00:24:35,433 --> 00:24:36,660
White Beard! Pirates!

325
00:24:47,860 --> 00:24:50,657
Sounds like they're pretty
pissed off down there?

326
00:24:50,740 --> 00:24:52,017
Scary!

327
00:24:52,100 --> 00:24:55,977
I want an update on the walls!

328
00:24:56,060 --> 00:24:57,720
Uh They're still down.

329
00:24:58,120 --> 00:25:01,002
Endeavor the energy that's
flowing into the city.

330
00:25:01,200 --> 00:25:03,740
Pump every ounce of power into the walls.

331
00:25:03,940 --> 00:25:04,920
Sir, right away.

332
00:25:09,580 --> 00:25:11,400
Almost there, Ace!

333
00:25:19,760 --> 00:25:20,590
Luffy!

334
00:25:20,880 --> 00:25:22,440
I'm coming for you!

335
00:25:24,100 --> 00:25:25,760
I'll save you!

336
00:25:27,140 --> 00:25:28,720
Activating full power!

337
00:25:41,640 --> 00:25:43,080
What is that?

338
00:25:45,340 --> 00:25:46,170
What?

339
00:25:46,320 --> 00:25:47,320
The walls!

340
00:25:54,260 --> 00:25:55,717
They've closed us in!

341
00:25:55,800 --> 00:25:57,660
What the hell's going on?

342
00:26:01,460 --> 00:26:02,580
Take this!

343
00:26:07,720 --> 00:26:08,960
Will daddy break?

344
00:26:10,100 --> 00:26:10,930
What?

345
00:26:12,840 --> 00:26:15,080
Oh man, not a scratch.

346
00:26:15,480 --> 00:26:18,009
That's gotta be some
seriously thick steel.

347
00:26:18,180 --> 00:26:19,860
I don't know about you guys,

348
00:26:20,020 --> 00:26:22,937
but I'm pretty sure these are the
walls they were talking about.

349
00:26:23,020 --> 00:26:23,850
Come on!

350
00:26:23,940 --> 00:26:25,764
Are you too scared to fight us?

351
00:26:29,380 --> 00:26:34,997
Hey look up there they've got an
arsenal of cannons locked on us we

352
00:26:35,080 --> 00:26:39,097
gotta run they've got us locked
in there isn't any place for us to

353
00:26:39,180 --> 00:26:45,537
except there what's going on down

354
00:26:45,620 --> 00:26:47,377
there why did it the last wall

355
00:26:47,460 --> 00:26:52,320
rage well it's uh it's oar's body
the walls don't seem strong enough

356
00:26:53,220 --> 00:26:54,057
to lift it, sir.

357
00:26:54,140 --> 00:26:59,022
Also, it looks like his blood is running
into the system and making it malfunction.

358
00:27:01,360 --> 00:27:02,480
Damn beast.

359
00:27:07,040 --> 00:27:08,960
Ores, you saved them.

360
00:27:13,260 --> 00:27:15,300
Now that's a noble death.

361
00:27:17,940 --> 00:27:20,177
He may be dead, but he's still fighting.

362
00:27:20,260 --> 00:27:21,201
Impressive, huh?

363
00:27:24,880 --> 00:27:25,710
Huh?

364
00:27:25,793 --> 00:27:27,500
You've given us a chance, Ours.

365
00:27:29,140 --> 00:27:30,517
We must be swift.

366
00:27:30,600 --> 00:27:32,500
You know what to do, Aka 'inu.

367
00:27:55,240 --> 00:27:56,800
Meteor Volcano!

368
00:28:11,960 --> 00:28:13,900
That's it! We're finished!

369
00:28:16,480 --> 00:28:18,320
They've got nowhere to run.

370
00:28:18,840 --> 00:28:22,260
Now we'll melt that
ice and drown them all!
